## 8. Fairness and customer experience

The audit compares how often groups are contacted (selection rate) under the recommended rule and under risk-only targeting, with bootstrap intervals and a risk-adjusted ratio ([fairness table](../reports/tables/fairness.csv)).

{% set senior = fairness_by[strategy ~ '|SeniorCitizen|1'] %}{% set female = fairness_by[strategy ~ '|gender|Female'] %}
- **Senior customers** are contacted {{ senior.ratio_to_reference | ratio(2) }} as often as non-seniors (95% interval {{ senior.ratio_lower_95 | num(2) }}-{{ senior.ratio_upper_95 | num(2) }}); after adjusting for churn-risk decile the ratio is {{ senior.risk_adjusted_ratio | ratio(2) }}. Seniors are more likely to churn ({{ senior.observed_churn | pct(0) }} vs {{ fairness_by[strategy ~ '|SeniorCitizen|0'].observed_churn | pct(0) }}) and are worth more on average ({{ senior.mean_customer_value | usd }} vs {{ fairness_by[strategy ~ '|SeniorCitizen|0'].mean_customer_value | usd }}), so expected value favours them. {{ "This is flagged for review: the gap is not fully explained by risk." if senior.review_flag and not senior.explained_by_risk else "The gap is largely explained by risk." }}
- **Gender:** ratio {{ female.ratio_to_reference | ratio(2) }} for women vs men (interval {{ female.ratio_lower_95 | num(2) }}-{{ female.ratio_upper_95 | num(2) }}){{ ", within the review band" if not female.review_flag else ", flagged for review" }}.
{% set loyalty_used = recommended_offer_mix | selectattr('offer_id', 'equalto', 'loyalty_reward') | list | length > 0 %}
- **Contract and tenure:** one- and two-year contract customers are almost never contacted because their churn risk is low; loyal customers receive fewer offers than new ones. Offers are benefits as well as contacts, so the catalog includes a loyalty reward{{ "" if loyalty_used else ", which the optimiser does not choose under current assumptions" }}; the playbook adds a non-targeted loyalty benefit and complaint monitoring for a "loyalty penalty" [[cma2020](references.md#cma2020)].
- **Error parity:** recall and calibration by segment are in [segment errors](../reports/tables/segment_errors.csv); groups under 50 customers are marked as small samples.

Policy: protected attributes are never model inputs or eligibility rules; any review flag goes to the Retention owner and the DPO before a wave is launched.

## 9. Assumptions

Save rate, offer and contact cost, margin, value horizon and discount rate are documented in the [assumption register](assumption-register.md) with sources and tested ranges. The value is a 12-month truncated proxy, not a validated lifetime value [[faderhardie2014](references.md#faderhardie2014)].

## 10. Limitations and external validity

- **No causal effect:** the data contain no randomised campaign. Expected values assume a save rate; high-risk customers may not be the most responsive [[ascarza2018](references.md#ascarza2018)] and contact can raise churn [[ascarza2016](references.md#ascarza2016)].
- **Sample data:** fictional US company; the churn label ({{ data.churn_rate | pct }}) is about 27 times real US monthly postpaid churn of about 1% [[verizon2026](references.md#verizon2026)]. Probabilities would need recalibration on real data; at {{ stress.targets[0] | pct(0) }} average churn only {{ stress.by['sample|' ~ ('%g' % stress.targets[0])].positive_ev_share | pct(0) }} of customers would be worth the standard offer ([stress test](../reports/analysis-report.md#outside-the-sample-lower-churn-and-vietnamese-prices)).
- **Single snapshot, random split:** no test of performance over time; tenure and charges are measured at the snapshot.
- **Vietnam:** the market is about 90% prepaid, where churn means inactivity or porting, not contract cancellation [[sggp2022](references.md#sggp2022)]; features such as contract type have no direct equivalent ([deployment note](deployment-vietnam.md)).
- **Value proxy:** no cost-to-serve, no plan-level margin, no re-churn after a save.

## 11. Monitoring and maintenance

See [governance-and-risks.md](governance-and-risks.md): monthly drift (PSI) and calibration (ECE, slope) checks, retraining at least every six months or when a trigger fires, and replacement of assumed save rates with pilot measurements.
